**Chapter 10, Section 19: "An Overwhelmingly Large Enemy"**

――Just how much time had passed since they started running?

In an environment where they couldn't properly feel the light from outside, and with an unknown amount of time spent unconscious, it was hard to say. But his gut feeling told him that anywhere from a few hours to half a day had passed since the incident began.

"Miraculously, it seems we've shaken off our pursuers..."

Catching his ragged breath and wiping the sweat dripping from his chin, Subaru looked back through the lukewarm stench, checking for any sign of the unseen footsteps of their pursuers.

Up until a little while ago, they'd been relentlessly chased by a group of royal soldiers, without a moment to rest. Their path had been blocked, their escape routes cut off, and the choices of being captured or forcing their way through had flickered repeatedly in his mind. All of those moments had been too close for comfort—but,

"We managed somehow, thanks to that ridiculously huge earthquake... Come to think of it, I don't remember ever experiencing an earthquake since coming here. What the hell was that?"

"Betty was surprised by that earth-shaking rumble too... but this is our chance, I suppose. Subaru, show me your arm. I'll put some healing magic on that burn."

"Oh, that's a lifesaver."

Saying this, Subaru lowered Beatrice, whom he had been carrying this whole time, onto the ground. Beatrice experimentally opened and closed her palm, then brought a faint healing light to Subaru's right arm—the arm wrapped in a handkerchief serving as a bandage. Feeling the persistent, throbbing ache ease, Subaru let out an involuntary sigh.

"I knew you were just putting on a brave front, I suppose. If you were in that much pain, I wish you would have said so sooner."

"No, seriously, while I was panicking and forgetting about it, the pain completely slipped my mind. The second I calmed down, it hit me all at once—owowow. H-Hurry... help me..."

"Yes, yes, what a hopeless child you are, I suppose. It'll be over in a moment, so don't you start crying."

"Thank you, Beako-mama! ...Is your mana situation pretty dire?"

"...To be frank, there's not much to spare, I suppose."

"...Well, yeah. Figured as much."

At Beatrice's reply as she treated his burn, Subaru scratched his cheek with his other hand. After all, it was unavoidable, considering the considerable display of power she'd put on at the Mathers estate. Shadow magic Minya, repeated Shamak, and on top of that, she'd even used E・M・T. With Subaru being such a pitiful external mana tank for her, she was likely on the verge of running on fumes.

It really made him want to lament his complete lack of aptitude for this other world.

"Though, I was in ridiculously good form back in the Empire... I wonder if it was some kind of deal where more dreams could be packed in when I was shrunk down?"

"That was an unnaturally distorted state where my Od was warped, so Betty doesn't have very good memories of it, I suppose. I can only imagine how many human experiments it took to make that possible."

"Even though he's not an enemy anymore and we've already left the Empire, the darkness of Olbart—or rather, the Shinobi—just gets deeper..."

Indeed, he couldn't imagine that kneading something like the Od—one's very soul—into any desired shape was something that could be done without practice. Which meant that Olbart, and the Shinobi village, had been practicing the kneading of souls. The name "Wicked Codger" held no falsehood.

"—It seems the soldiers are currently preoccupied dealing with the aftermath of that tremor from earlier. The alert presence mingled with the wind is growing distant; their tension has lessened. It's safe to assume we've shaken them off for the time being."

The one who joined the conversation then was Crusch, who had been surveying their surroundings with sharp eyes. Holding a dimmed Lagmite ore lamp to illuminate the sewer, she narrowed her amber eye, the one not covered by an eyepatch, and fell silent as she watched Subaru getting his arm treated.

For a moment, Subaru felt puzzled by her reaction, but he immediately realized what it was. The healing light—it must have reminded her of something familiar and unforgettable.

"...Now's not really the time to talk about that, huh."

Honestly, the situation was moving at a breakneck pace. For Subaru, ever since that scene with Al at the Pleiades Watchtower, things had been happening non-stop, one after another, giving him no time to rest his nerves. The rise of the "Divine Dragon's Church," Crusch's recovery, the subsequent commotion at the Mathers estate, and then becoming the fugitive Natsuki Subaru... it had been a total mess.

—The truth was, if he could have met with Crusch, he'd wanted to talk about Ferris's dismissal.

He had wanted to confirm the reason and true intention behind dismissing Ferris with Crusch, somehow find a point of compromise, and help mend the relationship between the two who had become estranged.

Surely, Ferris would call it arrogant meddling, but he didn't care. A man who was insufferably selfish and arrogant in the eyes of others—that was Natsuki Subaru.

"—To you all."

"...Hm?"

"To you all, I am grateful. For coming after me, in a situation like that."

At Crusch's words, spoken in a suddenly lowered tone, Subaru fell silent. To feel like this grueling half-day of constant running had been worthwhile just from that single "I am grateful"—even he thought that was selling himself cheap. But at the very least, if he hadn't made the choice to chase after her back in that moment, he wouldn't have been able to draw out those words just now.

"Still, I can't just casually say 'you're welcome' here. The burn hurts, and I guess Tea-ga protected me, but the whole fight started because of you in the first place, Crusch-san. And I'm definitely causing Emilia-tan and the others a ton of worry and trouble. And brave little Beako here has resolved herself to spend four hundred years of hell with me..."

"Subaru, Subaru, just because your thoughts are a mess, don't go ruffling Betty's head all over the place, I suppose. You'll ruin Betty's cuteness."

"Ah, sorry... You're right! What a disaster... it's unbearable to look at!"

"That's absolutely not the case, I suppose! Even if my hair is a mess, Betty's cuteness doesn't diminish; rather, it's the discovery of a new charm point, I suppose!"

Beatrice, her hair thoroughly mussed by Subaru's idle hands, shouted at him, unable to stop her treatment. That familiar exchange loosened the tension that had felt like it was knotted even in his organs, giving him a bit of relief. —Yes, it was just as Subaru was casually feeling that relief.

"Fufu."

"—! Did you just laugh, Crusch-san?"

A small sound that shook the air, and Subaru's eyes widened involuntarily. Looking over, he saw Crusch, standing by the dirty sewer wall, with her hand covering her mouth. She added a brief "Forgive me" under Subaru's gaze, then said:

"I couldn't help myself, watching that exchange so lacking in tension. How immature of me."

"I've got nothing to say back about the lack of tension, but it's way better than you being all wound up forever. We haven't been able to see anything but that scary look on your face for so long."

"A scary look, you say. This eye of mine has something to do with that, too."

"Hey, even with your eye like that, you're still a beautiful woman, Crusch-san."

"—"

"Subaru..."

"Huh?! Did I just make things awkward again?!"

Crusch, placing a hand on her eyepatch, narrowed her eye, and Subaru panicked under Beatrice's exasperated gaze. However, after a small sigh, Crusch slowly shook her head.

"You... no, you all are strong."

"If you're talking about me and Beako, you're right to use the plural. Me without Beako is just the best of the nobodies. But, y'know."

"But?"

"...It's a kind of strength you should have had yourself, Crusch-san."

At Subaru's answer, Crusch's lips pressed into a tight line. Seeing that, Subaru reflected on his words, wondering if he'd overstepped. The expression that had relaxed for just a moment had hardened again, because of him.

As he hesitated, wondering what to say next, Beatrice gave his arm a light pat.

"Here, it's done. For the time being, it should be fine, I suppose."

"Yeah? Thanks. ...Yeah, it feels a bit stiff, but not bad."

"Keep the handkerchief on, I suppose. It might get itchy, and your skin might get gooey, so be careful not to scratch it by accident."

"That's terrifying, so message received. —So, then."

Offering double thanks to Beatrice for giving him a well-timed breather, Subaru turned back to Crusch. His wound was treated, and they had shaken off their pursuers for the moment. That meant there was a mountain of things he wanted to talk to her about.

First, what he urgently needed to confirm was—

"Crusch-san, do you have any idea what to do in this situation? Anyone to turn to?"

"Anyone to turn to, you say. There was someone, before this happened. But, I cut that person down with my own hands."

"...The way you say that... could it be that the person you were counting on..."

"Indeed. It was Mathers MacMahon—before his sinister plot was exposed."

"Oh my god..."

At her matter-of-fact nod, Subaru felt the world darken before his eyes and looked up to the heavens, his gaze rebounding off the not-very-high, dirty sewer ceiling. Not that he was one to talk, since he'd been the same, but there were simply too many ways in which people sought to rely on Mathers for information within the Kingdom. The fact that even Crusch, placed in a difficult position as a royal election candidate due to the "Divine Dragon's Church" matter, had thought the same way spoke to Mathers's immense virtue.

However—

"That Mathers-san was harboring a conspiracy on the level of national subversion...?"

"Yes. Lord MacMahon welcomed my unexpected visit cordially. However, saying he had guests to receive, he had me wait in a separate room..."

"A separate room. And then?"

"I sensed a suspicious wind surrounding me in the guest room, and regarding the guest he was about to receive. Therefore, just as I was about to question his intentions, the people of the mansion stood in my way—and the rest is as you all know."

"What we saw..."

Being told the circumstances leading up to it—Mathers being cut down, servants and guards collapsed all over the mansion—even when explained again, it was still an answer he couldn't easily accept. In the end, the problem was that the only basis for Crusch's suspicion of Mathers and the others was a "suspicious wind"—in other words, it stemmed solely from her Divine Protection of Wind Reading.

"—"

It was obvious, but Subaru couldn't share the Divine Protection of Wind Reading that Crusch placed absolute faith in. So, aside from his desire to believe in Crusch, he couldn't hold any certainty.

And that was—

"—It's the same as me, back then."

Talking with Crusch, Subaru felt a tightening in his chest.

It was a situation in exact, complete reversal to the exchange he had once had with her—back when the royal election had just begun, when his eyes had been clouded by hatred for Petelgeuse Romanée-Conti, the Sin Archbishop of Sloth, who had caused devastating damage to the Roswaal mansion and Arlam Village. It was exactly the same situation.

"Back then, I was completely blinded by rage, my vision clouded by the fact that no one understood me. I couldn't listen to what anyone around me was saying at all..."

That distortion, clouded by hatred and fury, had been seen through by Crusch, who had then cut down his foolish, aggressive posturing without mercy. —This was a reenactment of that, but with their positions completely reversed.

Crusch's current words and actions were the same as Subaru's, when he had brandished information obtained through a method incomprehensible to others—Return by Death—and threw tantrums when no one understood him.

Of course, compared to the stupid Subaru of back then, Crusch appeared to be acting far more rationally. But unlike Subaru, who had been powerless, Crusch had both power and standing. And so—

"—Guess I can't do it, after all."

"...Subaru?"

"Once I realize you're in the same boat I was, I don't have the option of abandoning you here, Crusch-san. Whether it's to help you or stop you."

Subaru bit his lip and clenched his fist. Beside him, Beatrice quietly watched.

Back in those days, Crusch had been on the verge of the great undertaking of the White Whale's subjugation. Even so, she had patiently continued to engage with Subaru, who was ignorant, unreasonable, and rude. And in the end, she had listened to his words and lent her strength to help him achieve his great wish.

Now, it was Subaru's turn to do the same. —To stand beside her if she was right, and to stand in her way and stop her if she was wrong. For that purpose.

"Crusch-san, I—"

"—Wait, Natsuki Subaru."

Just as he was about to voice his firmly decided resolution, Crusch stopped him.

But her expression was too serious for him to think she was just dampening his spirits. She closed the distance between them, shielded Subaru and Beatrice behind her, and strained her eyes into the darkness of the sewer.

Even looking in the same direction as her vigilance, Subaru's eyes couldn't see anything, but—

"—Someone is there. Even if you hold your breath, emotions ride on the wind. You cannot escape my eye."

"—! But we should have shaken off the pursuing soldiers..."

"Someone with different intentions than them, I would guess. Let me say this clearly: remaining silent will bring you no benefit. Or, shall I assume you have hostile intentions and—"

"—Wait, wait, wait! Don't be hasty! Alright! I get it, alright!"

Just as Crusch, shortsword drawn before he knew it, was about to ready herself, a flustered voice came back from the darkness further down the waterway, prompted by her heightened tension and caution. After a moment of surprise that Crusch's eyes had been correct, Subaru frowned at the sound of the voice itself. "Huh?" —The voice was familiar.

"That voice just now..."

"Dammit! I'm coming over there now! You hear me? Don't you try anything! I've got absolutely no intention of fighting you bastards!"

"That depends on your actions. I must tell you I cannot make any rash promises. Though, you are alone and we are three. The numerical disadvantage is—"

"—Could it be... are you Chin?"

"What?"

As the man shouted, Crusch, not lowering her guard, raised an eyebrow at Subaru's question. Beatrice, drawing close to Subaru's side, also murmured quietly, "Chin..." and then added:

"That's the man we saw in Priestella, I'm pretty sure, I suppose."

"Yeah, that's right. He's being taken care of at Felt's place now..."

"—I'm here 'cause Felt told me to come, dammit. Tch, this ain't cool at all."

With that displeased click of his tongue, a man with his hands raised slowly emerged from the darkness.

Just as expected, it was a man with an even sharper glare than Subaru's—the glaring-eyed Rachins, one of the three back-alley stooges, Ton, Chin, and Kan, who had joined Felt's camp at some point.

"Whoa, Chin...! You never fail to deliver a fresh surprise every time you show up!"

"Shut the hell up! I told you before, my name ain't Chin! It's Rachins!"

"Chin, I suppose."

"I said it ain't Chin, you pipsqueak!"

"A foolhardy Chin, I suppose."

Ignoring Subaru's emotional reaction at seeing a familiar face for the first time in a while, Rachins and Beatrice engaged in a pointless argument.

Actually, he hadn't seen Rachins since Priestella—and even then, only during Sirius's rampage, which had triggered the Witch's Cult's abominable gathering. Of course, he had confirmed his safety afterward, but he was still glad to see him full of energy like this.

"Man, but I'm glad to see a familiar face. I've got things I want to ask you—"

"Stop right there, this 'Chin' person. Unlike Natsuki Subaru, I do not know you."

"Crusch-san?!"

In contrast to Subaru, who had reflexively rejoiced at reuniting with an acquaintance, Crusch's caution, as she fixed a sharp glare on Rachins with her shortsword in hand, hadn't eased in the slightest.

Come to think of it, Rachins hadn't been staying at the Water Plume Inn, and after they'd made contact with Sirius, he'd withdrawn from the front lines, so there hadn't been a chance for him to meet Crusch face to face. Crusch's caution seemed natural—but,

"Huh? You don't know me? For a Duchess of Karsten, you're pretty damn heartless."

"...What?"

"Well, sure, I ain't in a position to chat casually with lofty folks like a Duchess, but ain't you one of the people who learned swordsmanship from my old man? If you say you ain't got the slightest clue who I am, then my old man must not have done a very good job."

"—"

At Rachins's declaration, sticking out his long tongue, Crusch looked bewildered. Meanwhile, Subaru could only be completely dumbfounded by Rachins's sheer, brazen audacity.

"Hey, no matter how you look at it, that's a lie right off the top of your head..."

"It ain't no lie! ...Believe it or not, I come from a pretty decent family. The kind that, even if you can count 'em on one hand, has had meetings with a Duke's family and all."

"For real? If you're not for real, your delusions are seriously insane, man..."

That said, with him sounding so confident, it was starting to seem like the truth. A perfect example of how unreliable both people's hearts and words could be.

Partly because of that, Subaru timidly glanced over at Crusch.

"—. ————. ————————. Could you be the son of Sir Rickert Hoffman, who once served as the Royal Sword Instructor?"

"Ha! You hear that? Guess it stuck in the memory of the Duchess of Karsten after all."

"It's true?!"

"It appears to be true, I suppose."

Taking plenty of time, as if wringing the words out, Crusch spoke a single name. With Rachins's attitude confirming it, Subaru and Beatrice unconsciously exchanged glances.

To think Rachins really was from a Lugunica noble family.

"Then how come you're a back-alley thug who picks on the weak?"

"Shut your trap! Everyone's got their reasons, so quit digging!"

"We've got plenty of our own circumstances as well, I suppose. And it seems your reason for coming here isn't unrelated to those circumstances."

"Ngh...!"

"He's right. Just like Beako says. ...Crusch-san, please lower that. Chin's probably okay. I'll vouch for him."

"—. If I see a suspicious move or the wind blows, I will cut him down."

"Suspicious moves aside, how the hell am I supposed to take responsibility for the wind...!"

Faced with a trembling Rachins, Crusch slowly lowered her shortsword and relaxed her guarded stance. That said, she didn't go so far as to sheathe the blade, and her single eye remained fixed intently on Rachins's every move.

At any rate—

"Once again, thanks for coming. How did you find us?"

"Ain't any big method. It wasn't just me looking for you bastards. Gaston and Camberley are wandering around searching somewhere else, too."

"So, you just happened to draw the winning ticket? It really wasn't much of a method, I suppose."

"Shut it, pipsqueak. We found you, so it's fine, right? Argh, so? What the hell is goin' on with you guys?"

"About that, it's a long story, and I'm not confident you'd believe it. So let me hear your story first. —How are Emilia and the others?"

Knowing it was rude, Subaru pushed aside Rachins's question to ask his own.

After all, ever since escaping from the Mathers estate, he hadn't had a proper chance to get any information from the outside. His heart was already a mess of anxiety, worry, and impatience.

"The fact that we're together with Crusch-san should have reached Emilia and the others' ears by now. Which means we must be causing them a deathly amount of worry and trouble..."

A double burden: the mental burden of worry, and the physical burden of being questioned by the Kingdom. On top of that, their camp must be in considerable disarray. —However, Subaru's prediction was betrayed.

Completely, and in a way he never imagined.

"Ahh—"

"—?"

At Subaru's question, Rachins's glaring eyes widened slightly, and then, uncharacteristically, he put on an expression of concern for Subaru and said:

"That half-elf of yours has been taken into custody at the castle. And the others in your camp have fled and gone into hiding. —Just like you, they're all wanted now."








....





















"—Emilia's confinement at the royal castle, and the escape of Rem, Otto, and the others from the royal candidate's residence."

It was bad news that felt like the heavens and earth had been turned upside down.

Subaru chewed over the story Rachins had conveyed again and again, ruminating on it over and over so his brain could swallow every last bit of it whole. He piled effort upon effort, trying to somehow understand.

He tried, but—

"W-why did something like that happen...?"

"...Even Betty never expected this, not in the slightest, I suppose."

Utterly stunned, his face pale, Subaru noticed that his teeth were chattering uncontrollably. It seemed that events beyond comprehension could even rob a person of warmth. The blood circulating through his body had gone cold, to the point where he could almost feel the illusion of his fingertips and toes dying from frostbite.

Beside him, Beatrice gently held his hand, sharing her warmth. And yet, the trembling of his body wouldn't stop. —The situation was far worse than his shallow imagination had conceived.

"Because of... because of me, Emilia and everyone else..."

"Tch. I'm sure you wanna say some stupid crap like that, but stop actin' like this is all your fault. A situation like this—no matter how you look at it, you've been set up."

"Huh?"

With a sharp ringing in his ears and a wave of dizziness making him stagger, Subaru blinked involuntarily. At his reaction, Rachins crossed his arms and clicked his tongue in irritation.

He'd just said, as if it were the most obvious thing in the world, that Subaru and the others had been "set up."

"Set up... what do you mean by..."

"What do you mean, what do I mean? It's exactly what I said, ain't it? Hell, don't you think something's off? Too many inconvenient things are happenin' all over the place all at once."

To the dumbfounded Subaru, Rachins shrugged his shoulders with an exasperated sigh.

In place of Subaru, whose mind felt partially numbed and sluggish at Rachins's manner of speaking, Beatrice responded, "You mean..."

"Us being chased, Emilia being locked up in the castle... and such, I suppose?"

"—. It ain't just that. The reason the people in your camp just up and bolted without a word was probably 'cause they realized the other side's out for blood."

"Out for... blood?!?"

"It's a figure of speech, a figure of speech! They can't actually get away with suddenly killin' a royal election candidate. ...That's why even that brat could only send us out before she got hauled off, too."

As the dangerous word made Subaru's eyes widen, Rachins kicked the dirty wall. However, despite his brusque attitude, thanks to Rachins patiently explaining, Subaru's ability to think finally began to recover, little by little.

In short—

"Someone's pulling strings behind the scenes to knock Emilia out of the royal election. And my actions were used perfectly for that, getting Emilia captured in the castle. Otto and the others, realizing the intentions of whoever's scheming this, fled before they got their hands tied too... That about right?"

"Betty wants to add one thing to that, I suppose. —There's a possibility that Emilia isn't the only target of this villain."

"Not just Emilia?"

"————"

As Subaru raised an eyebrow at the observation, Beatrice nodded and jutted her chin. Following her motion, his gaze fell on Rachins, who wore a sour expression as he poked the inside of his cheek with his tongue.

It was, quite clearly, the face of someone who'd had an unpleasant point raised—

"...Could it be, Chin, that the reason you came isn't just because Emilia and Felt became friends?"

"Tch, damn pipsqueak... noticing extra crap..."

"Filling in for what Subaru lacks is Betty's role, I suppose. And... do you want to be taught a lesson over and over, pipsqueak... human?"

"Then teach your damn master here to call people by their proper names!"

Raising his voice at Beatrice, with whom he seemed to have particularly bad chemistry, Rachins heaved a deep sigh. Then, after hesitating for a moment,

"...It ain't just the half-elf from your camp that got nabbed at the castle. The Felt brat, too. They trumped up some charges, and even that bastard Reinhard's had his hands tied."

"Reinhard is?! And Felt was captured too... If that's true, then they're not just targeting Emilia, but the royal election itself?!"

"Took you long enough. She was suspicious about that, so before she got dragged to the castle, Felt gave us the order: 'Find big bro and the others. If you find 'em, don't leave 'em alone.' Thanks to that, we ended up runnin' around all over the place stinking of sewage."

It made sense that Rachins had been reluctant to talk about it, given it was a disadvantage for his camp, but having this information versus not having it completely changed the fundamental premise. Subaru had been convinced that his actions had been used for a personal attack against Emilia, but apparently, the enemy's aim was on an entirely different scale.

If Emilia and Felt, and by extension Subaru and Reinhard, and possibly even their respective camps were all in danger, then it was absolutely no coincidence. A secret maneuver targeting the royal election—a scheme to rock the Kingdom of Lugunica to its very core. And for a story of such an overwhelmingly large scale, Subaru just so happened to have heard something familiar.

"Crusch-san, did you hear that?! What you were saying..."

Lifting his head with renewed energy, Subaru turned the conversation toward Crusch, who had been watching the exchange.

Until Rachins joined them, Subaru hadn't been able to fully believe the legitimacy of Crusch's statements based on her Divine Protection of Wind Reading. But the rushing torrent of information now gave a certain persuasive power to those unconfirmed suspicions. It was even possible that the scheme by Mathers, which had driven Crusch to draw her sword, was connected to the malice trying to ruin the royal election.

However—

"...Hey, Crusch-san?"

There was no response. Wondering at this, Subaru looked at Crusch and couldn't believe his eyes. —Crusch, standing near the wall, was nodding off, her head bobbing drowsily.

To start dozing off in the middle of such an important discussion, and while on high alert no less, was an attitude far too out of character for her. As Subaru noticed and called out, Crusch looked back at him with clearly vacant eyes,

"...My apologies. A sudden wave of drowsiness. Most likely... a strain from this left eye, I think..."

"Strain? Wait... Since when has that eye..."

"I leave the rest... to you, Subaru...sama..."

"Hey—!"

As if reaching her limit, her upper body swayed unsteadily—and in the next instant, Crusch collapsed forward without warning. Hurriedly catching her limp body, Subaru saw the shortsword slip from her strengthless hand and fall to the stone floor of the waterway with a sharp clatter. But the sound meant nothing to her; she had already begun to breathe the quiet breaths of sleep.

"You've gotta be kidding me? Right in the middle of something this important... she fell asleep!"

"Oi, what's goin' on with the Duchess? They've been sayin' all sorts of things—she lost her memories, her body's messed up, and now her head's finally gone crazy."

"What?! Who the hell do you think you are, saying that about Crusch-san?! I'll knock your lights out, you bastard!"

"I ain't the one who said it! What the hell's wrong with you?!"

"Enough already, I suppose! Stop bickering over every little thing! —From the looks of it, she's simply asleep, I suppose. Just as the girl herself reported, her exhaustion seems to have broken its limits, I suppose."

Beatrice, who had stepped between Subaru and Rachins, gave her assessment as she peered at Crusch's sleeping face. To Subaru's eyes as well, the unconscious Crusch didn't seem to be in any particular distress; she simply looked like an utterly exhausted body seeking deep, heavy sleep.

However, as Beatrice had said, if this was a side effect of the Dragon Eye that Crusch had mentioned, then that unnatural thing was clearly something that shouldn't be left as it was.

More importantly—

"...The 'Divine Dragon's Church's' miracles, and Tea-ga's testimony. There's no way this situation, where royal election candidates are being targeted, is unrelated."

To put it bluntly, it was too much of a stretch to think these things weren't connected. But paradoxically, that led directly to suspecting the organization known as the Divine Dragon's Church.

The Divine Dragon's Church was a religion deeply and firmly rooted throughout the Kingdom of Lugunica. Even if they were to accept it as a hypothetical enemy, how far did that enmity extend?

Given the situation, he couldn't help but suspect Tea-ga, but then what about Sakura? —And Fiore?

"If my worst suspicions are right, I'll be devastated too, but Emilia's the one who's really going to be sad..."

Even without that, Emilia was currently confined in the castle, likely with no news of Otto and the others, much less the safety of Subaru and Beatrice. To alleviate even a little of that mental burden, he had to act. He had to make the optimal move.

With that determination, Subaru hoisted the sleeping Crusch onto his back, securing her firmly. While doing so, he exchanged a nod with Beatrice, who had retrieved the fallen shortsword and sheathed it.

"Rachins, we can't get anywhere here. Since you came all this way, you must know some place that's easier to talk, right? Let's move."

"I don't like bein' ordered around, but I'll let it slide without bitin' back this time. ...That said, I can't guarantee how well we can avoid prying eyes in the royal capital right now."

"...It really hits home all over again just how screwed this situation is."

The enemy was using a huge, truly immense power, scheming to ensnare Subaru and the others. The fact that they'd met up with Rachins here and been able to hear this from him was probably a miraculous stroke of incredibly favorable coincidence. Though, calling it a miracle might be an insult to Rachins, who had tracked them down on Felt's orders.

Regardless—

"I want to let Crusch-san rest somewhere safe as well. If she can find some peace, even a little, for body and mind, she should be able to talk more properly. So—"

"—Well, that's just perfect! For it was precisely at this very moment, this very instant, that I have been wanting, absolutely dying, to extend an invitation to the fugitives currently throwing the entire royal capital into chaos...!"

"—What?!"

In an instant, a voice completely at odds with the surroundings echoed through the sewer. Subaru, with Crusch on his back, along with Beatrice and Rachins, all stiffened, their eyes widening as they spun around.

The voice had come from beyond the darkness of the waterway, where the meager light of the Lagmite ore couldn't reach. But toward that spot, Rachins clicked his tongue—"Tch"—and threw something.

"Ooh, let there be light! Kuhahahaha, how very thoughtful, how very considerate!"

A hard sound echoed against the stone floor of the sewer, and in the next moment, a white light brilliantly illuminated the darkness. What he'd thrown was a Lagmite ore itself—the type that emitted light upon impact.

Just as Rachins, with his split-second decision, had intended, it exposed the figure hiding in the darkness to the view of Subaru and the others as they turned.

It was—

"...A mask?"

"Now, now, now. For your first impression of me to be 'a mask'—isn't that a little too exactly what you see, plain as day? Show a little more creativity, won't you? Choose your words as passionately and fervently as if trying to woo the woman of your dreams! Kuhahahahaha!"

So saying, the figure shook with booming laughter—a man, and that was all that could be discerned, other than that he was tall. For the man wore a black robe that completely enveloped his entire body, and on his face, he wore a mask resembling that of a jester.

The white jester's mask, floating hazily in the darkness, made his abnormality all the more pronounced. His words, his attitude, the sinister gaze directed at them from behind the mask—after an encounter of a mere five seconds, it was instantly clear. —This masked jester was no good, at all.

As if to prove it—

"Feel free to die, all of you. My business is only with the woman sleeping there!"

In that instant, the darkness of the sewer was lit up by a massive blaze, incomparable even to the light of the Lagmite ore, and a colossal wave of heat surged toward Subaru and the others.
